WEBVTT

02:12.770 --> 02:16.064
Good evening and welcome to our council meeting on May 21,

02:16.236 --> 02:20.210
2025. I'd like to acknowledge this week is National

02:20.710 --> 02:24.250
Public Works Week, where we celebrate our wonderful public works teams

02:24.750 --> 02:28.530
that bring essential services and programs to our community. Their impact

02:28.610 --> 02:32.850
is inestimable. With our staff contributing to keeping

02:33.350 --> 02:35.970
our roads safe, ensuring quality drinking water,

02:36.510 --> 02:39.790
building facilities and maintaining infrastructure for our growing community,

02:40.590 --> 02:43.310
managing and maintaining our fleet of cars,

02:43.810 --> 02:46.910
trucks and emergency vehicles, stewarding our waterways,

02:46.990 --> 02:50.390
trees and environment, optimizing our landfills

02:50.890 --> 02:54.310
and waste collection, and above all, advancing the quality of life for

02:54.810 --> 02:57.910
all. Now call on Will Short, our regional clerk,

02:58.410 --> 03:01.230
to conduct the roll call. Thank you, Chair. Chair Redman. Present.

03:01.470 --> 03:04.630
Councillor Craig. President. Councilor Erb. Present.

03:04.790 --> 03:07.510
Councilor Foxton. Present. Councilor Harris.

03:08.870 --> 03:09.990
Councilor Hunick?

03:12.310 --> 03:15.670
I don't know. Oh, yes, it is. Present. Councillor James.

03:18.790 --> 03:21.990
I see you, but we can't hear you. Councilor Liggett. Present.

03:22.710 --> 03:26.070
There we go. Councilor Liggett. Thank you. Councilor McCabe.

03:26.310 --> 03:30.400
Councilor Nowak. Councilor Rodrigues. Present. Councillor Solenon.

03:31.680 --> 03:35.600
Councillor Schantz. Present. Councilor Vrbanovic. Here. And Councillor Wolf.

03:36.100 --> 03:36.800
Present. Thank you, Chair.

03:40.720 --> 03:44.280
I'd like to acknowledge that the land that we gather on today is

03:44.780 --> 03:48.200
a traditional territory of the Haudenosaunee, the Anishinaabe and the Chonnonton

03:48.700 --> 03:51.800
peoples. In doing so, I want to reflect on what it means to be doing

03:52.300 --> 03:56.080
important community work that we are engaging in collectively today and

03:56.580 --> 03:59.360
also in my own. In individual relationship to this land.

04:00.160 --> 04:03.800
As a settler, one of the most important aspects of my individual journey

04:04.300 --> 04:08.320
towards truth and reconciliation has been to listen. And I am continually

04:08.820 --> 04:13.000
grateful that the community shares their stories and concerns with me as

04:13.500 --> 04:16.920
well. As chair of the region, I know I carry a large responsibility to ensure

04:17.420 --> 04:20.720
that it is not just myself as an individual listening and acting,

04:20.800 --> 04:24.120
but that as a government, we are listening and creating action within

04:24.620 --> 04:28.110
the community. I am offering this acknowledgement as one of the

04:28.610 --> 04:32.830
many actions I am personally and the region largely is taking on our journey towards

04:33.330 --> 04:36.830
reconciliation. We acknowledge the enduring presence

04:37.330 --> 04:40.670
of the indigenous people with whom we share this land today, their achievements and

04:41.170 --> 04:44.670
their contributions to our community. Are there any

04:45.170 --> 04:46.430
declarations of pecuniary?

04:46.930 --> 04:50.310
Interesting, seeing none.

04:50.810 --> 04:53.590
We have no presentations. We do have delegations.

04:55.830 --> 04:59.510
I will take them as they're listed on the agenda. And if you're

05:00.010 --> 05:03.350
attending in person, please proceed to the podium where you will be called on to

05:03.850 --> 05:07.630
speak. You have five minutes to speak if you registered before the deadline

05:08.130 --> 05:11.750
and three minutes if you registered afterwards. Additionally, some general

05:12.250 --> 05:15.670
reminders. If you conduct yourself in any of the following manners, it will result

05:16.170 --> 05:20.210
in an immediate removal from the meeting. Interrupting councillors,

05:20.710 --> 05:24.690
staff or other delegations. Derogatory statements about councillors,

05:25.190 --> 05:29.170
staff or others Turning your camera on at inappropriate times

05:29.250 --> 05:31.490
or hate speech or defamatory comments.

05:32.930 --> 05:36.370
One last reminder for delegations, please do not take offense

05:36.870 --> 05:40.330
if following your presentation, there are no questions from council. This is

05:40.830 --> 05:44.330
council's time to really listen and reflect upon the opinions and ideas shared

05:44.830 --> 05:48.330
with us from our community members. And a quick reminder to members

05:48.830 --> 05:52.190
of the audience, you are asked to maintain order and this means you may

05:52.690 --> 05:56.430
not address council without permission of the Chair. Interrupt anyone,

05:56.670 --> 06:00.350
Disrupt the meeting with unreasonable noise or vocal expressions such as

06:00.850 --> 06:04.670
applause, booing or cheering or displaying signs or posters.

06:05.470 --> 06:09.510
Our first delegation is Tanner Bergsma from Waterloo.

06:10.010 --> 06:13.390
Tanner, if you come to the podium, you have five minutes

06:13.890 --> 06:14.750
and the floor is yours.

06:22.200 --> 06:25.680
Thank you. Thank you. Good evening,

06:26.180 --> 06:29.760
Chair, council members and members of the public. My name is Tanner bergsma.

06:30.260 --> 06:33.680
I'm a 22 years old autistic student, multinational activist and former

06:34.180 --> 06:38.040
homeless youth. This evening I'm here to respectfully request that the regional

06:38.200 --> 06:41.520
council consider the inclusion of an additional clause within the current

06:42.020 --> 06:45.200
motion to address the urgent and ongoing housing crisis in our

06:45.700 --> 06:49.340
community. I speak from lived experience. I came from nothing.

06:49.660 --> 06:52.700
I spent nearly two and a half years without stable housing,

06:52.780 --> 06:56.260
sleeping in sidewalks, stairwells and in overcrowded

06:56.760 --> 07:00.620
shelters with no space left. I know firsthand what it feels like to be

07:01.120 --> 07:04.460
reduced to a statistic. To be cold, hungry and unseen

07:04.960 --> 07:08.140
by the very systems designed to provide protection and support.

07:08.700 --> 07:12.060
And I'm 19 years old. Whilst I was trying to survive, I lost

07:12.560 --> 07:15.050
my daughter. So I'm not here tonight for recognition.

07:15.770 --> 07:19.370
I'm here because I've seen what happens firsthand when we fail to act.

07:19.770 --> 07:23.530
I've seen people freeze to death on these streets. And I'm here to say

07:23.690 --> 07:27.690
survival should never be the benchmark we set for human dignity.

07:28.570 --> 07:31.610
Since April of 2024, someone that I know,

07:32.110 --> 07:35.210
an elderly resident of this region, has been living in their car.

07:35.770 --> 07:39.130
They have now frostbite on their feet.

07:39.650 --> 07:43.450
That's not a distant story. That's not a statistic. That is

07:43.950 --> 07:47.410
happening right now, here in this region while

07:47.910 --> 07:50.530
luxury condo towers just rise blocks away.

07:51.090 --> 07:53.810
That is not fortunate. This is inhumane.

07:54.610 --> 07:58.450
We talk about economic strain, affordability and uncertainty

07:58.950 --> 08:01.970
in the motion before you. And you're right, people are struggling.

08:02.370 --> 08:06.320
But while we discussed inflation and tariffs, let's not forget that

08:06.820 --> 08:10.320
some people don't even have a front door to lock behind them.

08:10.720 --> 08:14.080
Waterloo region has received millions in federal

08:14.240 --> 08:17.760
housing funding, yet there is still no clear immediate

08:18.260 --> 08:21.600
plan to address the housing crisis. Thousands are being left behind.

08:21.920 --> 08:25.200
We are not facing a housing challenge as stated in the committee

08:25.700 --> 08:29.280
report. This is a housing emergency. One that is structural,

08:29.360 --> 08:32.980
moral and political. When a young person sleeps in a stairwell,

08:33.480 --> 08:36.860
when a mother moves from couch to couch with her kids, when a senior must

08:37.360 --> 08:39.100
choose between a bed and her meal,

08:41.580 --> 08:44.940
this is not moral. This council should not be focused

08:45.440 --> 08:49.420
on optics. It should be focused on action. The current pace of luxury development

08:49.500 --> 08:52.980
is widening the gap between rich and poor, while the social fabric of

08:53.480 --> 08:57.660
our community is being torn apart. You are building a region where developers flourish

08:58.160 --> 09:01.420
and vulnerable people are left to suffer in silence. That is not

09:01.500 --> 09:03.820
government governance, that is neglect.

09:04.380 --> 09:07.700
So tonight I'm here to respectfully ask that the Council add a specific

09:08.200 --> 09:12.060
amendment to the motion brought forward by the Administration and Finance Committee. One that is

09:12.560 --> 09:16.300
small, realistic and urgently needed. Quote, that urgently.

09:16.800 --> 09:19.940
Council directs staff to engage individuals with

09:20.440 --> 09:23.500
lived experience of homelessness alongside local service

09:24.000 --> 09:27.900
providers to co develop a clear, time bound, affordable and supportive housing

09:28.400 --> 09:31.620
action plan by the end of 2025. End quote. Let the people

09:32.120 --> 09:36.180
who have lived through it help shape the solution. You already

09:36.680 --> 09:40.100
have experts who can tell you what needs to happen. You just need to listen.

09:40.260 --> 09:44.260
I'm willing to help. I will sit at that table. I will help you reach

09:44.760 --> 09:48.140
the people whose voices are too often left out of the room because I've been

09:48.640 --> 09:52.420
one of them. This addition would strengthen your emotion. It would make sure that

09:52.920 --> 09:55.700
housing stays a core part of this region's plan to protect the vulnerable,

09:55.940 --> 09:59.550
especially in times of economic uncertainty. You talk about stimulus

10:00.050 --> 10:03.870
strategies. Let's make sure that these strategies don't just build concrete, they build

10:04.370 --> 10:07.390
our community. Let's make sure growth means everyone rises,

10:07.890 --> 10:11.750
not just those at the top. Everyone deserves a chance at a life

10:12.250 --> 10:16.390
in society. We have that duty. We have the responsibility as

10:16.890 --> 10:20.390
leaders to uplift our community. Because if we don't take care of our people,

10:20.550 --> 10:24.190
there won't be a strong region to build. There won't be anyone

10:24.690 --> 10:27.870
left. You cannot grow a future. Tanner. You have one minute left.

10:27.950 --> 10:31.350
Thank you. You cannot grow a future on frozen sidewalks and

10:31.850 --> 10:35.350
forgotten lives. So I'll end with this. If it were your child

10:35.850 --> 10:39.070
sleeping in that sidewalk, if it were your child sleeping

10:39.230 --> 10:42.510
in that stairwell, if it were your mother freezing in that car,

10:42.750 --> 10:46.070
would you wait for another study? Or would you act like their

10:46.570 --> 10:50.190
life depended on it? Because for hundreds of people in this region, it does.

10:50.790 --> 10:53.990
Thank you. Thank you, Tanner. We have a

10:54.490 --> 10:58.030
question. Councillor Huinink. Thank you, Chair Redman. Thank you, Tanner, for your delegation.

10:58.530 --> 11:01.830
I'm just wondering if you're familiar with the co creators table,

11:02.330 --> 11:05.430
which is part of the plans and critical business, and how

11:05.930 --> 11:09.830
your suggested addition to the motion

11:10.330 --> 11:14.070
would differ from that. Yes, that is a great question.

11:14.790 --> 11:18.800
That action plan as far as to date has

11:19.300 --> 11:22.920
not been implemented quick enough. And my concern is

11:23.420 --> 11:26.920
that the committee is not hearing the

11:27.420 --> 11:31.640
people. We are seeing that we have to remove the

11:31.800 --> 11:35.320
people from the homeless encampment by December 1st

11:35.480 --> 11:38.760
with no clear action or plan on how we are going to do so.

11:39.320 --> 11:42.600
I'm just requesting that this council by also

11:43.100 --> 11:46.480
working with the people and working with staff and working

11:46.980 --> 11:50.320
with the people in the encampments, we can find a solution that works.

11:50.960 --> 11:53.960
Okay, thank you. Thank you. Thank you, Tanner.

11:54.460 --> 11:57.040
I have no further questions. Thank you for coming in and sharing your thoughts.

11:57.680 --> 12:01.200
The next delegation is Stephen Palmateer, co chair,

12:01.360 --> 12:04.600
Wilmot Civic Action Group. Welcome,

12:05.100 --> 12:07.840
Stephen. You have the podium and you have five minutes.

12:10.650 --> 12:15.090
Five minutes means I must have registered

12:15.590 --> 12:19.050
on time. I think

12:19.550 --> 12:23.290
in the agenda it says I'm going to be speaking about Honda's pause

12:23.790 --> 12:26.970
and growth at their Alliston plant. Actually only going

12:27.470 --> 12:30.770
to touch on that because there's been lots going on

12:31.270 --> 12:34.250
in our community since I registered.

12:36.200 --> 12:40.240
Most recently, Chair Redmond, your interview last

12:40.740 --> 12:44.200
week with the Kitchener Record. I'd like to begin with that

12:44.600 --> 12:47.000
interview with Louise d' Amato.

12:47.800 --> 12:51.440
It reminds me a lot of Margaret Thatcher. You remind

12:51.940 --> 12:56.000
me a lot of Margaret Thatcher. Very powerful woman. Does anybody do

12:56.500 --> 12:59.800
this? If you know a lot of young faces in the crowd. Anybody? Margaret Thatcher

13:00.600 --> 13:02.600
mostly over here. Not so much over here.

13:04.600 --> 13:06.920
The Iron Lady. She was called the Iron Lady.

13:08.120 --> 13:12.360
Her catchphrase being, there is no alternative.

13:13.320 --> 13:17.520
And she was called the Iron lady because she'd stick to her policies regardless

13:18.020 --> 13:21.520
of what her constituents wanted, regardless of the impacts to

13:22.020 --> 13:25.560
her parliamentary democracy, regardless of sound

13:26.060 --> 13:27.960
reason or impact on the people she ruled over.

13:29.410 --> 13:32.770
There is no alternative is a great way

13:33.270 --> 13:36.650
to retroactively excuse any decisions that you

13:37.150 --> 13:39.570
make because it seems as though they were inevitable.

13:40.690 --> 13:43.410
Keep that in mind. All your young people over here with Tanner.

13:44.690 --> 13:48.450
You're probably going to hear lots of reasons why the encampment.

13:48.950 --> 13:52.290
We just couldn't move fast enough. It was inevitable. There was no alternative.

13:52.930 --> 13:56.700
But you'll find that things move very, very quickly when

13:58.860 --> 14:02.860
those in power want them to move very, very quickly.

14:03.900 --> 14:06.140
Anyway, returning to the interview,

14:07.180 --> 14:11.660
Louise d' Amato she begins, this is a major, highly controversial

14:12.160 --> 14:15.660
development. She's referring to the Wilmot Land assembly, yet it's rolling

14:15.740 --> 14:19.900
full speed ahead without a single public meeting or

14:20.400 --> 14:24.210
any information from the public about the costs, financial or

14:24.710 --> 14:28.410
otherwise. That made me raise my eyebrow. What other costs might

14:28.910 --> 14:32.810
there be besides financial costs? Our ability to

14:33.310 --> 14:36.650
grow food, the quality of our drinking water, Is that a

14:37.150 --> 14:41.250
financial cost? The public's trust in our democratic institution,

14:41.750 --> 14:45.650
is that a cost? But there is no

14:45.890 --> 14:48.470
alternative, is there? Chair Redman,

14:51.020 --> 14:54.900
you respond to Louise. We're very confident we'll continue because all the

14:55.400 --> 14:58.860
due diligence we've done thus far points in the direction of continuing the assembly.

15:00.140 --> 15:03.820
Due diligence? The same due

15:04.320 --> 15:08.380
diligence that was exhibited when you hired a mercenary cash cropper from

15:08.880 --> 15:13.020
Strathroy outside of our region, paid him in our tax dollars

15:13.500 --> 15:17.180
to shred standing corn a month prior to its harvest.

15:17.650 --> 15:21.290
Is that due diligence now? In some

15:21.790 --> 15:25.490
cases, the topsoil is simply washing away into the storm drains. Has there been any

15:25.990 --> 15:29.570
due diligence on the liability that that may cause? Downstream in Brant

15:30.070 --> 15:33.409
county, they don't have a groundwater aquifer like we do to

15:33.909 --> 15:37.370
filter their drinking water, so they have to pay to filter out the sediment that

15:37.870 --> 15:41.410
we're washing down the drain at present. And in fact,

15:41.650 --> 15:45.230
now I think you're renting some of that land back

15:45.730 --> 15:49.150
to some farmers who are currently out in those fields, perhaps not in the rain,

15:49.650 --> 15:53.030
but at this time of year planting those fields again.

15:54.310 --> 15:57.910
Why bother hiding behind phrases like due diligence? Why not

15:58.410 --> 16:01.590
simply tell us what Margaret Thatcher knew 50 years ago?

16:02.150 --> 16:05.030
There is no alternative.

16:06.550 --> 16:10.070
Louise D' Amato continues, and she asks why the public doesn't

16:10.570 --> 16:14.030
know how much public money has been spent on this project. And then she

16:14.530 --> 16:16.450
continued by asking, when would they know?

16:17.490 --> 16:20.970
You replied, Chair Redman, how would that change the

16:21.470 --> 16:25.450
context? Stephen, you have one minute remaining. I don't know that having a price tag

16:25.950 --> 16:27.170
at this juncture would make any difference.

16:29.570 --> 16:33.130
I think that's ridiculous on its face. Chair Redman, a price

16:33.630 --> 16:36.530
tag at this juncture would make all the difference, even if it didn't account for

16:37.030 --> 16:40.330
things like drinking water. But I'll return to water perhaps in a moment,

16:40.830 --> 16:44.550
although I've got very little time left. Let's continue with your interview. There are

16:45.050 --> 16:48.550
so many things changing in our community. You said we're growing and we've

16:49.050 --> 16:52.470
got new investment and new markets and new supply change. I got very,

16:52.970 --> 16:56.910
very confused at this new investment. In the same interview, you said we lost

16:57.410 --> 17:00.750
10 billion in investment over the past five years because we

17:01.250 --> 17:03.830
lacked a large industrial site. Well, first of all, we don't lack a large industrial

17:04.330 --> 17:06.910
site. We have the east side lands. In fact, they're closer to the Grand River.

17:07.410 --> 17:12.499
The existing highways like the 401, the Breslau Airport, the existing railways are

17:12.999 --> 17:15.539
we. We've got new investment and yet we've lost 10 billion.

17:16.499 --> 17:20.019
What new markets are you referring to? What new supply chains? You continue.

17:20.339 --> 17:23.859
I know the European Union is looking at new trading partnerships. Stephen, would you like

17:24.359 --> 17:28.459
to sum up. You're out of time. Let's sum up by

17:28.959 --> 17:33.419
quoting Mike Farwell, someone whom I've disagreed with publicly on this, and yet he continues

17:33.919 --> 17:37.299
in the Record today. That's not the way a transparent

17:37.799 --> 17:41.130
organization operates. Any questions? I don't

17:41.630 --> 17:45.330
see any questions, Steven. Thank you. So,

17:45.830 --> 17:45.970
colleagues,

17:49.250 --> 17:52.730
this is the end of this evening's delegations. The next agenda

17:53.230 --> 17:56.730
item is minutes of previous meetings. I would now entertain a motion

17:57.230 --> 18:01.650
to approve the minutes of Previous meetings listed 6.1 to 6.11,

18:02.450 --> 18:05.850
moved by Councilor Huinink, seconded by Councilor Harris. Please use your

18:06.350 --> 18:07.610
E scribe to vote it.

18:44.580 --> 18:47.980
Thank you, colleagues. That is carried under communications.

18:48.480 --> 18:51.700
There's item 7.1 and 7.2 that are received for

18:52.200 --> 18:57.100
information for your reference. The Council package as

18:57.600 --> 19:00.020
of May 14th was distributed to you electronically.

19:01.160 --> 19:04.760
I see. No questions. The next agenda item is a motion

19:05.260 --> 19:09.160
to go into the committee. The whole. I would entertain a move removed

19:09.660 --> 19:12.840
by Councilor Nowak, seconded by Councilor Vrbanovic.

19:13.340 --> 19:16.640
Please use your E scribe to vote that the Council go into committee of the

19:46.210 --> 19:48.210
Councillor Liggett, are you in favor? Thank you,

19:49.810 --> 19:53.730
colleagues. That carries the first report under consideration

19:54.230 --> 19:57.940
is finance, and it is regarding the 2026

19:58.440 --> 20:02.260
plan and budget process and the principles. And then we'll vote on the

20:02.760 --> 20:07.380
remaining finance items, the plan for 2026

20:07.880 --> 20:11.860
and the budget process and principles. I want to clarify that the report for

20:12.360 --> 20:16.020
the 2026 budget plan process was referred from May

20:16.153 --> 20:19.340
6, 2025. Committee meeting. There was a

20:19.840 --> 20:23.220
motion associated with this report moved by Councilor Hunick and seconded

20:23.720 --> 20:27.920
by myself, that added a third clause. Direct budget

20:28.420 --> 20:31.800
issue papers for any budget increases that include additional

20:32.300 --> 20:36.200
FTEs to align with this referral. That is the motion that will

20:36.700 --> 20:40.040
be considered along with the report tonight. Are there any questions of

20:40.540 --> 20:41.960
clarification before we proceed,

20:46.200 --> 20:49.400
Councillor Foxton? No, Councillor Salonen,

20:50.440 --> 20:53.560
thank you. Through you, Chair, two things. One,

20:53.640 --> 20:58.230
on what you were just mentioning about the

20:58.730 --> 21:01.870
third item of directing staff presents a budget issue paper.

21:02.110 --> 21:06.070
I was just curious on the wording and this could have been my misunderstanding

21:06.570 --> 21:10.310
from committee. I thought it was to have a business case for

21:10.810 --> 21:14.750
each fte, so I was hoping to seek clarity on that

21:15.310 --> 21:18.750
part. I would agree with your recollection. So if

21:19.250 --> 21:22.510
it's clear we'll say business case instead of issue paper because that is.

21:23.160 --> 21:25.000
That is exactly the words that were used.

21:25.880 --> 21:30.240
Okay, thank you. And then the other one if I

21:30.740 --> 21:32.560
don't know if you want me to move it now but I did have a

21:33.060 --> 21:36.880
question for close pertaining to an identifiable individual in relation to

21:37.380 --> 21:41.160
this report. So if we could move a motion to go into

21:41.660 --> 21:44.480
closed. I don't know. You have other colleagues though I can't see everyone around the

21:44.980 --> 21:48.720
horseshoe. If anybody has other questions, I'm going to go through all the other

21:49.220 --> 21:52.720
questions and then I'll see how colleagues feel about going into close

21:53.220 --> 21:57.060
because there wasn't one schedule at Councillor Salonen. So I'll hold that in a

21:57.300 --> 21:58.740
bance councelor sh.

22:00.660 --> 22:04.020
I'm not sure if I'm in the right report but does, does this

22:04.740 --> 22:06.740
where we are, include the schedule?

22:07.540 --> 22:11.140
Okay. Yes it does. I just want to note that November

22:11.640 --> 22:15.540
18th is one of our council meeting nights and that's

22:16.040 --> 22:20.380
listed as a public meeting. So if that would be the woolage public meeting that

22:20.880 --> 22:23.060
would be a problem. I'm not sure which one it is.

22:29.880 --> 22:33.080
Can we make a note of it and we'll make an adjustment. Thank you

22:33.640 --> 22:37.200
Councillor Foxton. Thank you. I just wanted to thank you for the changes in the

22:37.700 --> 22:39.960
schedule. But I agree with Councillor Schontz, so you're already aware.

22:44.440 --> 22:46.920
Thank you Councilor Huinink.

22:47.720 --> 22:50.120
Thank you Chair Redman, in regard to the budget,

22:51.280 --> 22:54.080
