01:42:25.450 --> 01:42:29.970
The next agenda item is Board of Health and

01:42:30.470 --> 01:42:34.850
I Now call on Dr. Wong, Commissioner of Public Health and Paramedic Services, Medical Officer

01:42:35.350 --> 01:42:38.690
of Health to provide a verbal update. Dr. Wong is

01:42:39.190 --> 01:42:42.490
on camera because she's sick, so thank you for

01:42:42.650 --> 01:42:45.970
protecting the rest of us and I hope you get well soon. Over to

01:42:46.470 --> 01:42:49.530
you, Dr. Wong. Thank you, Chairman and good evening members

01:42:50.030 --> 01:42:53.610
of Council. Thank you for the opportunity to present a Board

01:42:54.110 --> 01:42:56.930
of Health update with information about measles,

01:42:57.570 --> 01:43:01.650
the latest drug alert and vector borne

01:43:01.730 --> 01:43:05.490
diseases. First, with respect to measles,

01:43:06.370 --> 01:43:10.090
we continue to see an increase in measles activity locally

01:43:10.590 --> 01:43:14.420
and provincially is now circulating in

01:43:14.920 --> 01:43:18.620
our community. As of end of day Yesterday,

01:43:19.100 --> 01:43:23.140
we had 78 confirmed cases and 22

01:43:23.640 --> 01:43:26.820
probable cases, local and provincial

01:43:27.320 --> 01:43:30.820
cases continue to primarily be in those who are

01:43:31.320 --> 01:43:33.420
unvaccinated or under immunized.

01:43:34.860 --> 01:43:37.322
As of May 13,

01:43:37.718 --> 01:43:41.260
1622 cases of measles have been reported

01:43:41.420 --> 01:43:43.560
across 18 local public health agenc,

01:43:44.910 --> 01:43:48.470
with 182 new cases reported in

01:43:48.970 --> 01:43:52.670
the week preceding that. Last week, two local high

01:43:53.170 --> 01:43:57.270
schools closed due to measles exposures. Public Health

01:43:57.770 --> 01:44:01.550
worked closely with the school boards to support their staff and students to return

01:44:02.050 --> 01:44:05.830
to school, and both reopened Tuesday after the long

01:44:06.330 --> 01:44:09.950
weekend. Measles symptoms, as a reminder, begin seven

01:44:10.450 --> 01:44:13.920
to 21 days after infection and may include high

01:44:14.420 --> 01:44:17.080
fever, cough, runny nose,

01:44:17.640 --> 01:44:21.360
red watery eyes and a red rash lasting four

01:44:21.860 --> 01:44:25.320
to seven days. Measles can cause serious illness

01:44:25.820 --> 01:44:28.599
and death. Infants under one year of age,

01:44:28.760 --> 01:44:32.080
unimmunized pregnant individuals and people with weakened

01:44:32.580 --> 01:44:35.160
immune systems are at increased risk of complications.

01:44:35.880 --> 01:44:39.720
For those who are fully immunized, the risk of infection and

01:44:40.220 --> 01:44:42.280
hospitalization is very low.

01:44:43.800 --> 01:44:47.720
Earlier this month, Ontario's Ministry of Health expanded

01:44:48.220 --> 01:44:52.000
eligibility for measles vaccine for all of western Ontario,

01:44:52.500 --> 01:44:56.440
including Waterloo region. This expanded eligibility

01:44:56.680 --> 01:45:00.240
covers babies and children from 6 months

01:45:00.740 --> 01:45:04.730
to 5 years of age who can now receive measles vaccines earlier.

01:45:06.090 --> 01:45:10.690
In addition, adults born on or after 1970 can

01:45:11.190 --> 01:45:14.810
now receive a second dose of vaccine if they do not already have

01:45:15.210 --> 01:45:18.370
have one. To get the vaccine,

01:45:18.870 --> 01:45:22.730
residents are encouraged to reach out to their primary care provider or access

01:45:23.230 --> 01:45:27.610
walk in clinics. Public Health will also be hosting some

01:45:28.110 --> 01:45:31.530
clinics for priority groups without access to a primary care provider.

01:45:32.120 --> 01:45:35.440
These clinics will begin June 2 and appointments for

01:45:35.940 --> 01:45:38.360
those clinics will be posted on our website shortly.

01:45:39.880 --> 01:45:43.320
There are steps residents can take to protect themselves and their families.

01:45:43.560 --> 01:45:46.680
1. Ensure you are up to date with measles vaccinations.

01:45:47.320 --> 01:45:51.280
2. Monitor yourself and your family for signs and symptoms of

01:45:51.780 --> 01:45:56.520
measles, especially after returning from international travel

01:45:57.020 --> 01:46:01.150
or areas experiencing measles outbreaks. And finally,

01:46:01.650 --> 01:46:04.870
if you develop symptoms, limit contact with other people. In particular,

01:46:04.950 --> 01:46:08.390
do not attend school, childcare or healthcare settings.

01:46:09.030 --> 01:46:12.950
Call your healthcare provider or walk in clinic and notify them about your

01:46:13.450 --> 01:46:16.790
symptoms before the appointment so they can take precautions

01:46:17.590 --> 01:46:21.310
before you come. Wear a medical mask when seeking

01:46:21.810 --> 01:46:25.310
care. Next, an update about the

01:46:25.810 --> 01:46:29.070
latest Drug Alert. A community Drug Alert

01:46:29.570 --> 01:46:32.390
is issued by the OMARS Collaborative.

01:46:32.470 --> 01:46:36.550
OMARS is short for Overdose Monitoring Alert

01:46:37.050 --> 01:46:40.710
and Response System and is a collaborative of community

01:46:40.790 --> 01:46:44.310
agencies, public health, paramedic services

01:46:44.810 --> 01:46:48.630
and police. An alert is issued when partners

01:46:49.110 --> 01:46:53.190
have observed an increased number of overdoses within a

01:46:53.590 --> 01:46:57.270
short period of time. This may signal an

01:46:57.770 --> 01:47:00.310
elevated risk for people who use drugs.

01:47:01.430 --> 01:47:05.270
While it is not usually possible to pinpoint the exact

01:47:05.750 --> 01:47:09.270
reasons behind an increase. We do know

01:47:09.770 --> 01:47:13.230
that changes in the toxicity of the drug supply can

01:47:13.730 --> 01:47:18.110
lead to an increased risk for users in

01:47:18.610 --> 01:47:22.270
an illegal drug supply. These changes can occur at any

01:47:22.770 --> 01:47:26.210
time. In terms of overdose trends

01:47:26.710 --> 01:47:31.170
that we are monitoring, between April 1 and

01:47:31.670 --> 01:47:35.690
May 20 of this year, paramedic services responded to

01:47:36.190 --> 01:47:39.530
fewer overdose drug poisoning calls

01:47:40.030 --> 01:47:44.250
compared to the same time period in 2024 and

01:47:45.290 --> 01:47:48.530
2023. And so far,

01:47:49.030 --> 01:47:53.210
the number of suspected drug related Deaths reported in 2025

01:47:53.840 --> 01:47:55.840
is similar to 2024.

01:47:57.760 --> 01:48:01.320
And finally, an update about vector

01:48:01.820 --> 01:48:05.880
borne diseases. As the weather gets warmer,

01:48:06.380 --> 01:48:10.080
we expect to see the annual seasonal increase in

01:48:10.580 --> 01:48:14.040
vector borne diseases. Vector borne diseases like West

01:48:14.540 --> 01:48:18.000
Nile virus and Lyme disease are carried by

01:48:18.500 --> 01:48:22.560
vectors such as mosquito and ticks and

01:48:23.060 --> 01:48:26.560
can be acquired by humans from mosquito and tick

01:48:27.060 --> 01:48:30.760
bites. Public health conducts vector borne disease

01:48:31.260 --> 01:48:34.640
surveillance, vector source reduction

01:48:35.119 --> 01:48:38.960
and provides public education to reduce the risk of vector borne

01:48:39.520 --> 01:48:43.120
illness in Waterloo region. And finally,

01:48:43.620 --> 01:48:47.160
last week, municipalities were notified of mosquito larva sighting

01:48:47.660 --> 01:48:50.590
activities across the region which will begin in June.

01:48:51.790 --> 01:48:54.990
And that's it for my update and I'd be happy to take any questions.

01:48:59.230 --> 01:49:02.950
Thank you Dr. Wong, Councillor Huinink. Thank you Chair Redman and

01:49:03.450 --> 01:49:07.070
thank you Dr. Wong for presenting. Even though you're sick, we hope

01:49:07.570 --> 01:49:11.910
you get better very soon. I'm just wondering where can the

01:49:12.410 --> 01:49:16.070
public and or members of council go if, if they want to check

01:49:16.230 --> 01:49:20.150
the list of exposure sites in Waterloo region for the measles.

01:49:20.790 --> 01:49:24.230
Oh, thank you, Councillor Huinink. So we keep that

01:49:25.510 --> 01:49:28.870
list constantly

01:49:29.370 --> 01:49:32.150
updated in real time on our website.

01:49:32.950 --> 01:49:37.590
So if you go to regionofwaterloo Ca

01:49:39.270 --> 01:49:43.160
measles you will arrive at a landing page about

01:49:43.660 --> 01:49:46.920
measles and there you can find the link to all

01:49:47.420 --> 01:49:51.360
the exposure sites in Waterloo region, public exposure sites.

01:49:51.440 --> 01:49:54.640
Great, thank you. And this might sound a bit funny, but I am

01:49:55.140 --> 01:49:59.280
serious. I give my dog, flea and tick medication to prevent tick bites.

01:49:59.440 --> 01:50:03.200
Is there something at all similar for human beings

01:50:06.010 --> 01:50:09.610
really in terms of protection? It is

01:50:10.110 --> 01:50:13.690
to try to prevent the bites in the first place from

01:50:14.190 --> 01:50:18.570
the mosquitoes or the tick. So often it has to do with preventative actions like

01:50:19.610 --> 01:50:23.050
the type of clothing you wear, checking your body

01:50:23.550 --> 01:50:26.890
after you go out into the woods and

01:50:27.290 --> 01:50:30.730
putting on insect repellent. And for

01:50:30.810 --> 01:50:34.600
West Nile, trying to get rid of standing water

01:50:35.100 --> 01:50:39.040
sites on your property. So it's really actions

01:50:39.540 --> 01:50:43.600
that are geared towards trying to prevent the mosquito

01:50:44.100 --> 01:50:47.240
or tick bites. Or if you know, you do find, for example, a tick on

01:50:47.740 --> 01:50:53.240
your body, is to remove it if

01:50:53.740 --> 01:50:55.760
you see it on your body. Okay, thank you.

