01:51:47.830 --> 01:51:49.370
of those harder to reach populations.

01:51:51.220 --> 01:51:54.900
Sure. Thank you for the question, Councillor McCabe. So yes,

01:51:55.400 --> 01:51:58.900
in southern Ontario or western Ontario there are

01:51:59.780 --> 01:52:04.180
communities that generally,

01:52:04.680 --> 01:52:08.660
you know, don't believe in vaccination and have not been taking

01:52:08.740 --> 01:52:12.660
up vaccination. And you know, the province has found

01:52:12.820 --> 01:52:16.390
that, you know, measles is spreading

01:52:16.890 --> 01:52:18.590
in particular in these populations.

01:52:20.350 --> 01:52:24.990
And the efforts have been made in all local areas experiencing

01:52:26.110 --> 01:52:28.830
increases in cases, including ours,

01:52:29.470 --> 01:52:33.150
with members of these

01:52:33.470 --> 01:52:37.750
communities and their leadership to

01:52:38.250 --> 01:52:40.270
try to encourage increased vaccination.

01:52:42.680 --> 01:52:46.160
Otherwise there are also, you know, like you mentioned,

01:52:46.660 --> 01:52:50.120
some people who may not be up to date with their vaccines. What we've

01:52:50.620 --> 01:52:54.040
noticed in the current situation in western Ontario

01:52:54.600 --> 01:52:58.320
is really that most of

01:52:58.820 --> 01:53:00.840
the cases are in children.

01:53:02.200 --> 01:53:05.000
And so that is why,

01:53:05.400 --> 01:53:09.110
you know, even though we, we had an increase in measles that

01:53:09.610 --> 01:53:13.110
we were responding to, Public Health

01:53:13.610 --> 01:53:17.230
also continued its efforts with respect to the enforcement of

01:53:17.730 --> 01:53:21.510
the Immunization of School Pupils act and the clinics that were

01:53:22.010 --> 01:53:26.390
offered to try to catch up students on their vaccinations because

01:53:26.470 --> 01:53:30.070
again, the core, you know, the core

01:53:32.230 --> 01:53:36.370
method of slowing down measles

01:53:36.870 --> 01:53:40.290
spread is to have a highly

01:53:40.770 --> 01:53:44.690
immunized population because if it's in a population

01:53:44.850 --> 01:53:48.410
where there's not a lot of immunization, it will spread extremely

01:53:48.910 --> 01:53:53.090
quickly. But when it encounters a population with high

01:53:53.590 --> 01:53:57.090
rates of immunization, the virus spread will start to

01:53:57.590 --> 01:54:00.610
significantly slow down. So you know,

01:54:01.110 --> 01:54:05.010
while there are obviously measures that public health will do

01:54:05.490 --> 01:54:09.130
in the immediate term, as we're doing now, to try to control case

01:54:09.630 --> 01:54:12.690
and contacts, the most

01:54:13.190 --> 01:54:17.010
important longer term strategy is to increase the immunization

01:54:19.090 --> 01:54:22.570
of children and students in

01:54:23.070 --> 01:54:26.380
our area. So that's why that

01:54:26.880 --> 01:54:30.540
continues to be the core measure that we need to focus

01:54:30.620 --> 01:54:34.940
on. And what we have seen in our region is that generally

01:54:35.180 --> 01:54:38.900
overall when we do the enforcement of the

01:54:39.400 --> 01:54:43.380
school of immunization, sorry, the enforcement of the

01:54:43.880 --> 01:54:48.060
immunization of School Pupils Act. We raise the immunization

01:54:48.300 --> 01:54:51.850
rates back to where they

01:54:52.350 --> 01:54:55.450
should be overall for schools in

01:54:55.950 --> 01:55:00.210
our region. So we do maintain a relatively

01:55:00.710 --> 01:55:03.410
good immunization rate in the general population,

01:55:04.930 --> 01:55:09.730
but there continues to be spread in

01:55:11.010 --> 01:55:15.090
a much greater spread and much greater number of cases and contacts

01:55:15.250 --> 01:55:19.370
in communities that don't uptake immunization.

